{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission.json\", \"summary\": \"Draft updated at submission.json (validated read-only: valid, no diagnostics) with the harness assurance_generated_test.go, and the scratch copy removed. This turn executes the discriminator registered for the membership question: investigation b87d04b254e44ceaadb200304929056a-question-0 now has an experiment whose four probes run through the real MsgProp path on freshly elected three-voter clusters with the leader in a simple configuration, with the harness also playing the application (advancing applied, driving the messages the state machines produce until quiescence, and running the type-based apply loop with panics recovered). Predicate as declared: a conf change proposal is either admitted (its entry keeps a conf-change payload) or rejected (the call reports an error), never silently replaced by an unrelated empty normal entry. Comparisons: the empty-change-in-simple-config probe and the second-proposal-while-unapplied probe carry the predicate (expected violated), with DisableConfChangeValidation as the bypass control that must keep the conf-change payload, and a valid single-node addition as the positive control that must commit and reach the applied configuration. Construction-time local runs show, for the record and not as formal evidence, that the failing proposals return a nil error while the appended entry at the proposed index is an EntryNormal with zero-length data and pendingConfIndex is left unset, that the valid addition keeps its payload, sets pendingConfIndex and reaches voters {1,2,3,4}, and that the bypass probe keeps the payload but would panic ('can't leave a non-joint config') if the application applied it. Counterevidence stays explicit: the conversion is deliberate, guarded by DisableConfChangeValidation and announced only through a library log line, so the question is scoped to whether the proposal result alone can establish admission; the formal conclusion awaits the controller's retained execution receipt.\"}"}}
